---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import { Capability } from '../components/Foundation.jsx';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
---
<Site title="Technology"><PageIntro title="The context behind every configuration." text="Model research, remote execution, and inference optimization connected through existing, traceable workflows."/>
<section class="section technical-stack"><article id="research"><div class="chapter-number">01 / Research</div><div><h2>Evidence before execution.</h2><p>Nemotron assists model research and assessment using Hugging Face metadata and sourced Tavily research. Claims retain source URLs and verified, inferred, or unknown status.</p><p>Selection pins an immutable model revision. A research assessment does not establish that a model runs in a particular engine or image.</p><div class="artifact-example"><code>requirements → sources → assessment → selected revision</code><span>Research and runtime validation remain distinct.</span></div></div></article><article id="execution"><div class="chapter-number">02 / Execute</div><div><h2>Remote work, explicit ownership.</h2><p>The validation workflow submits worker payloads to Nebius Serverless AI Jobs. Workers produce inference measurements and artifacts for ingestion and reporting.</p><p>Optimization takes a separate path: Infiro prepares the request; the existing LLM Optimizer controller owns optimization GPU jobs, checkpoints, and result collection.</p><a class="text-button" href="/architecture">Explore the execution branches →</a></div></article><article><div class="chapter-number">03 / Optimize</div><div><h2>Search serving settings.<br/>Keep the workload fixed.</h2><p>The optimizer explores framework-specific configuration dimensions. Input/output lengths, prompt count, request concurrency, and seed stay attached to each comparison.</p><p>Default objectives are mean E2E latency and mean TTFT at concurrency one; at higher concurrency, output-token throughput and mean E2E latency. Supported scalar studies can use pruning under the existing restrictions.</p></div></article></section>
<Capability client:visible />
<section class="section content-section"><h2>Strategies are tools, not promises.</h2><div class="capability-grid inner-grid"><article><h3>TPE</h3><p>A model-based sampler that uses observed outcomes to guide future proposals. Its behavior depends on budget and configuration.</p></article><article><h3>Gaussian process</h3><p>A surrogate-based approach useful for exploring smooth objectives. Availability depends on the optimizer’s optional dependencies.</p></article><article><h3>Random and grid</h3><p>Useful baselines and systematic exploration strategies. They are not Bayesian optimization.</p></article></div><p class="muted small">The public lab uses actual seeded Optuna samplers offline. It does not emulate engine execution or establish which sampler wins on inference workloads.</p><a class="text-button" href="/demo/search">Compare the search traces →</a></section>
<section class="section content-section"><h2>Compatibility is specific.</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Technology</th><th>Existing role</th><th>Qualification</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>vLLM · SGLang · TensorRT-LLM</td><td>Optimization preparation profiles</td><td>Verify the selected model, engine version, and worker image.</td></tr><tr><td>Nemotron</td><td>Research and assessment</td><td>Evidence confidence is separate from runtime support.</td></tr><tr><td>Nebius Serverless AI</td><td>Remote validation and optimization execution</td><td>Credentials, resources, and correct images are required by existing workflows.</td></tr><tr><td>Dynamo</td><td>Inference ecosystem reference</td><td>No Dynamo execution adapter is claimed in this repository.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><Callout /></Site>
